WEBVTT

00:00:00.255 --> 00:00:04.778
Mia, I push this toy trolley, stretch
a spring, and squash a foam block.

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:06.928
What do these actions have in common?

00:00:07.677 --> 00:00:10.051
Forces, pushes or pulls.

00:00:10.392 --> 00:00:13.208
They can change motion or
shape even though the force

00:00:13.208 --> 00:00:15.088
itself is not a visible object.

00:00:15.891 --> 00:00:16.671
Exactly.

00:00:16.938 --> 00:00:19.535
A force has both magnitude and direction.

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.485
We measure it in newtons,
symbol N, using equipment such

00:00:23.486 --> 00:00:25.066
as a calibrated newton meter.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:28.650
Our diagram arrows show
direction and relative size.

00:00:29.349 --> 00:00:32.199
So kilograms would be the
wrong unit for the force arrow.

00:00:32.616 --> 00:00:37.675
A longer arrow means a larger force only
if the diagram uses a consistent scale.

00:00:38.495 --> 00:00:42.183
Sort these into forces that require
contact and forces that act at a

00:00:42.184 --> 00:00:47.177
distance: tension in a string, friction,
gravity, and magnetic attraction.

00:00:48.019 --> 00:00:50.607
Tension and friction are contact forces.

00:00:50.949 --> 00:00:54.573
Gravity and magnetic forces act
without the objects touching.

00:00:55.003 --> 00:00:57.757
Electrostatic forces can
act at a distance too.

00:00:58.563 --> 00:00:58.910
Good.

00:00:59.304 --> 00:01:02.998
The normal contact force acts
perpendicular to a supporting surface.

00:01:03.321 --> 00:01:05.658
A rope under tension
pulls along its length.

00:01:06.890 --> 00:01:10.888
Upthrust is the force a fluid can
exert upwards on an immersed object.

00:01:11.574 --> 00:01:13.454
Normal does not mean ordinary here.

00:01:13.786 --> 00:01:15.971
It means at right angles to the surface.

00:01:16.147 --> 00:01:19.621
So on a slope, it is not
necessarily vertically upwards.

00:01:20.017 --> 00:01:22.171
A book rests on a horizontal table.

00:01:22.465 --> 00:01:24.611
Draw only the forces acting on the book.

00:01:24.938 --> 00:01:26.265
What goes on our diagram?

00:01:27.034 --> 00:01:31.167
Its weight acts downwards, and the
table's support force acts upwards.

00:01:31.572 --> 00:01:36.280
If those are its only vertical forces and
it is not accelerating, they are equal.

00:01:36.978 --> 00:01:37.535
Correct.

00:01:37.921 --> 00:01:41.285
Do not mix forces on different
objects into one resultant.

00:01:41.646 --> 00:01:45.967
The book's force on the table belongs
on the table's diagram, not the book's.

00:01:46.771 --> 00:01:49.816
And the table is not merely
holding the book without any force.

00:01:50.182 --> 00:01:53.873
Its contact force matters even
when nothing visibly moves.

00:01:54.587 --> 00:01:59.206
A trolley has a 30 newton force to
the right and 12 newtons to the left.

00:01:59.589 --> 00:02:00.758
What is the resultant?

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.177
Eighteen newtons to the right.

00:02:03.736 --> 00:02:08.785
I subtract opposite directions and state
the direction rather than just writing 18.

00:02:09.561 --> 00:02:10.344
Exactly.

00:02:10.597 --> 00:02:12.467
Forces in the same direction add.

00:02:12.981 --> 00:02:17.227
With forces in several directions, we
must account for each direction rather

00:02:17.227 --> 00:02:19.305
than add every magnitude blindly.

00:02:19.646 --> 00:02:23.052
Resultant means the combined
force acting on that object.

00:02:23.783 --> 00:02:26.586
If all forces balance,
the resultant is zero.

00:02:27.196 --> 00:02:29.396
Does that mean the object
must be stationary?

00:02:30.017 --> 00:02:30.386
No.

00:02:30.787 --> 00:02:34.428
It can remain stationary or keep
moving at constant velocity,

00:02:34.639 --> 00:02:36.430
constant speed in a straight line.

00:02:37.032 --> 00:02:41.063
A resultant force changes velocity,
which can mean speeding up, slowing

00:02:41.064 --> 00:02:42.881
down, or changing direction.

00:02:43.658 --> 00:02:48.350
A car traveling round a bend can have
constant speed but changing velocity,

00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:50.712
so it still needs a resultant force.

00:02:51.487 --> 00:02:52.267
Exactly.

00:02:52.577 --> 00:02:56.802
Also, zero resultant force is
not the whole story for rotation.

00:02:57.136 --> 00:03:00.335
Forces can balance overall
yet produce a turning effect.

00:03:00.681 --> 00:03:02.648
We will meet that when we discuss moments.

00:03:03.166 --> 00:03:05.376
Our bag has a mass of two kilograms.

00:03:05.812 --> 00:03:09.560
We take the same bag to the moon
without adding or removing material.

00:03:09.937 --> 00:03:10.824
What changes?

00:03:11.551 --> 00:03:14.537
Its weight changes because the
gravitational field is weaker.

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:16.913
Its mass remains two kilograms.

00:03:17.285 --> 00:03:19.460
Mass and weight are not interchangeable.

00:03:20.267 --> 00:03:20.821
Correct.

00:03:21.126 --> 00:03:25.568
In this course, mass describes the amount
of matter and is measured in kilograms.

00:03:25.943 --> 00:03:29.049
Weight is gravitational
force measured in newtons.

00:03:29.420 --> 00:03:32.452
Weight equals mass times
gravitational field strength.

00:03:33.217 --> 00:03:38.131
Using 10 newtons per kilogram for
Earth, two times 10 gives 20 newtons.

00:03:38.476 --> 00:03:39.587
Using 1.6

00:03:39.590 --> 00:03:41.461
for the moon gives 3.2

00:03:41.461 --> 00:03:42.091
newtons.

00:03:42.847 --> 00:03:43.246
Good.

00:03:43.632 --> 00:03:46.493
Earth's surface value is approximately 9.8

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:49.966
newtons per kilogram, often
rounded to 10 in questions.

00:03:50.332 --> 00:03:52.073
Always use the value supplied.

00:03:52.432 --> 00:03:55.274
Mass can change if matter
is added or removed.

00:03:55.665 --> 00:03:58.836
Merely changing location does
not change this bag's mass.

00:03:59.621 --> 00:04:03.015
Astronauts float in orbit because
there is no gravity there, right?

00:04:03.804 --> 00:04:06.463
That is our next imaginary lost mark.

00:04:06.958 --> 00:04:09.883
Gravity still acts strongly
in low Earth orbit.

00:04:10.118 --> 00:04:13.764
The spacecraft and astronauts are
falling together around Earth, so they

00:04:13.764 --> 00:04:15.981
experience very little supporting force.

00:04:16.796 --> 00:04:20.044
Their apparent weightlessness is
not evidence that gravitational

00:04:20.045 --> 00:04:21.209
attraction vanished.

00:04:21.968 --> 00:04:22.788
Exactly.

00:04:23.258 --> 00:04:26.830
And if air resistance is negligible,
objects released together in the

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:30.438
same gravitational field have the
same gravitational acceleration

00:04:30.673 --> 00:04:32.240
regardless of their masses.

00:04:32.686 --> 00:04:35.532
Different air resistance helps
explain why a feather falls

00:04:35.535 --> 00:04:37.162
differently in ordinary air.

00:04:37.621 --> 00:04:40.080
Friction always slows
the whole object down.
